1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Ah, you're finally awake, slave Troyard.

2
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:13,880
Where am I?

3
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:19,600
You are in my castle, and you are safe now. Take your time and rest.

4
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:21,840
What happened? How did I get...

5
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:26,480
I remember being interrogated by Count Cruteo, but...

6
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:30,600
You have nothing more to fear from him. I have dealt with Count Cruteo.

7
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:35,980
My lord, are you saying... that you have killed Count Cruteo?

8
00:00:36,380 --> 00:00:39,720
Your father is a man to whom I owe a great debt.

9
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:43,500
Accordingly, I am bound by honor to repay it.

10
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:45,200
A debt?

11
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:52,120
Fifteen years ago, when war broke out, I was given the assignment of landing on Earth as a scout for the Empire.

12
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:57,760
While there, I was caught in Heaven's fall and suffered massive, life-threatening injuries.

13
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:04,820
When the moon was sundered and the Earth's crust was deformed, there was no haven where any of us could turn for help.

14
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:11,740
When I was found by your father, Dr. Troyard, he did not even hesitate to help. My life was saved by his care.

15
00:01:12,020 --> 00:01:13,180
Father did that?

16
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:17,600
And now I have seen just how deeply your loyalty to the princess runs.

17
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:24,840
I find it utterly admirable how you managed to conceal her survival so the assassins were not aware of the fact.

18
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:28,200
My lord, how did you know that Her Highness was alive?

19
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:31,780
Slain, you should understand that Count Cruteo is not a traitor.

20
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:35,820
He has proven his loyalty and truly meant his oath to the princess.

21
00:01:35,820 --> 00:01:44,140
But that is not the case for me. I am the one who plotted every attempt against her, and I will kill her.

22
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:45,540
Huh?

23
00:01:45,540 --> 00:02:15,520
I am the one who plotted every attempt against her.

24
00:02:15,540 --> 00:02:45,520
I am the one who plotted every attempt against her.

25
00:02:45,540 --> 00:03:15,520
I am the one who plotted every attempt against her.

26
00:03:15,540 --> 00:03:25,860
Pay attention to your surroundings, and also don't forget your infrared, and keep a sharp lookout.

27
00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:28,520
Yes, ma'am. Showing three bogeys, two o'clock.

28
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:34,220
But there's no IFF signal. Flagging is hostile. They're nearly in weapons range. Engaging now!

29
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:43,000
Wow, look at that. Yuko's really good. She's like a one-woman militia.

30
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:47,560
Yep, she's got pretty good instincts, no question about that. Are you here to get some practice in, too?

31
00:03:47,660 --> 00:03:50,380
Come on. You know that I got assigned to the maintenance crew.

32
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:52,080
Well, for the moment, anyway.

33
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:55,140
Wait, you mean that there could possibly be an opening?

34
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:58,580
You have to remember, this is a war.

35
00:04:01,020 --> 00:04:02,380
Why don't you let me try?

36
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:06,380
Hey, sniper girl, what's up?

37
00:04:06,420 --> 00:04:09,060
I thought you said you haven't had any military training before.

38
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:10,280
I played a lot of games.

39
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:14,080
Hey, was one of them SimCat 10? That game's absolutely sick!

40
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:18,480
I'm only so-so at live drills, but I kick ass at that game.

41
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:21,880
I'm impressed you learned to pilot the real thing from a game.

42
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:29,960
Those Martians!

43
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:33,180
Can't tell by looking at them that they're not from Earth,

44
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:35,780
so there's no way to know till they come clean about it.

45
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:39,640
Inaho's been such a major jerk about this.

46
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:42,520
He knew who she was, and he wouldn't even tell his friends.

47
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:46,180
Well, I guess my baby brother is finally starting to grow up.

48
00:04:46,540 --> 00:04:49,120
Would have been nice if he'd confided in his big sister, though.

49
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:51,520
Now that he's found a girl he really likes...

50
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:51,720
What?

51
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:55,100
Huh? What do you mean? What'd you just say?

52
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:56,600
Given the times we live in,

53
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:59,180
a Martian wouldn't exactly be met with open arms.

54
00:04:59,620 --> 00:05:01,660
But if he had a real princess in his life,

55
00:05:01,780 --> 00:05:04,600
that means we'd all be related to a family of royals.

56
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:05,360
Uh, whoa.

57
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:08,260
Is that really true? Is that what he's gonna do?

58
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:10,860
Come on now, romantic stuff and your brother?

59
00:05:10,860 --> 00:05:12,860
He's not even smiling at her or anything.

60
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:15,800
He's just wearing the same standard grumpy look.

61
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:17,400
He's different now, completely.

62
00:05:17,780 --> 00:05:18,840
You really think so?

63
00:05:18,940 --> 00:05:21,220
I'm family. I always know what's going on.

64
00:05:21,440 --> 00:05:24,280
I see when he's happy, or when he's depressed and low,

65
00:05:24,420 --> 00:05:25,940
or when he's telling me a lie.

66
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,600
That is his on-cloud-nine face.

67
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:30,620
Sure about that?

68
00:05:30,620 --> 00:05:31,640
Think about it.

69
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:34,440
My emotionless nerd brother listening to every word

70
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:36,440
coming out of a girl's mouth is not standard.

71
00:05:36,620 --> 00:05:37,600
You got a point there.

72
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:39,520
Well, for him, it's the ultimate expression

73
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:40,860
of how much affection he feels.

74
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:41,940
Lord, Dr. Kaiska!

75
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:44,900
Permission to take a break now!

76
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:45,500
Go ahead.

77
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:46,840
Hey, wait for me!

78
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:51,160
So can I give it a try?

79
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:52,860
Sure, why not? Climb on in.

80
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:55,760
If you're sure you don't want to join the others.

81
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:02,440
Are you really able to tell?

82
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:06,580
When someone is lying to you?

83
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:07,900
Yeah, pretty much.

84
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:09,840
Like right now, for instance.

85
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:12,280
You're covering up something, aren't you?

86
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:14,080
A Martian.

87
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:17,260
And she's a princess, too.

88
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:20,860
Guys sure do love taking on a challenge, don't they?

89
00:06:21,280 --> 00:06:22,740
Well, I wouldn't worry about it.

90
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:23,960
You've got as good a chance with him

91
00:06:23,960 --> 00:06:25,200
as anybody else here does.

92
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:27,540
It makes me feel great that my little brother

93
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:28,840
is so popular with the girls.

94
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:33,500
This map shows the 26 landing castle drop points

95
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:36,440
confirmed by the UFV before contact was lost.

96
00:06:37,780 --> 00:06:40,640
But there are 37 clans in the Mars Knights.

97
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:43,240
There's a possibility that other landing castles

98
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:44,200
have made Planet Ball.

99
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:46,680
And Intel suggests a possibility

100
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:48,940
their forays are mostly in urban areas.

101
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:52,140
Therefore, we can minimize the possibility

102
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:54,720
of enemy encounters by routing our flight

103
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:56,240
through low population areas

104
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:58,340
and at low altitude to avoid radar.

105
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:01,640
Commander Mizusaki.

106
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:03,460
Ma'am, would you like to know

107
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:05,480
why you have such difficulty getting a date?

108
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:06,420
Uh, yes.

109
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:09,200
Possibility, possibility, possibility.

110
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:12,120
If you do nothing but play it safe

111
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:13,280
when opportunity arises,

112
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:15,260
you'll likely never meet Mr. Wright.

113
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,020
I was given to understand

114
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:18,660
one should first form a bond, ma'am.

115
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:19,500
All right.

116
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:20,960
Let's go with your

117
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:24,720
I-want-to-make-steady-progress-toward-my-goal-without-any-excitement approach.

118
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:26,940
So then you don't approve?

119
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:30,200
I think it's a very safe and well-thought-out plan.

120
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:39,640
She doesn't like it.

121
00:07:46,640 --> 00:07:47,920
Sim target destroyed.

122
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:50,040
Okay then, simulation's complete.

123
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:51,420
Ryei, isn't it?

124
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:52,300
Congrats.

125
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:54,500
You gamers have a pretty intense set of skills.

126
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:56,120
Increase the difficulty.

127
00:07:56,120 --> 00:08:00,580
Listen, maybe we should just call it a day.

128
00:08:00,780 --> 00:08:01,420
I'm fine.

129
00:08:01,660 --> 00:08:02,260
Keep going.

130
00:08:02,640 --> 00:08:03,020
Hmm.

131
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:04,280
Okay.

132
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:07,100
I'll throw in something we came up against a little while ago.

133
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:08,800
Try this out.

134
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:10,860
Begin simulation.

135
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,380
Thermal signature detected.

136
00:08:16,780 --> 00:08:17,760
It's on my ten.

137
00:08:17,980 --> 00:08:19,220
Target almost in range.

138
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:42,360
Watch it, Ryei.

139
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:43,160
Don't do that.

140
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:44,580
You'll overheat the gun barrel.

141
00:08:44,580 --> 00:08:44,960
Ah!

142
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:51,800
Simulation terminated.

143
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:52,860
I'm sorry.

144
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:55,140
I made it too difficult, too quick.

145
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,300
Sorry if it threw you.

146
00:08:58,500 --> 00:08:59,880
Warrant officer Kaiska.

147
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:01,800
Oh, hey, Dr. Yagurai.

148
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:03,900
How's that servo assist working out?

149
00:09:04,340 --> 00:09:05,920
Want to do a little arm wrestling?

150
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:07,300
No, I don't think so.

151
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:11,280
Actually, I was hoping I could borrow your simulator program a little later.

152
00:09:11,620 --> 00:09:14,220
Are you planning on going into combat now, Doc?

153
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:17,240
No, definitely not doing that.

154
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:19,820
I need it for a treatment plan.

155
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:24,320
Damn it to hell.

156
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:25,980
I can't believe it.

157
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:29,300
Our captain turns out to be your kid's sister, Huma Ray.

158
00:09:35,780 --> 00:09:38,360
Well, that probably explains where she gets her guts.

159
00:09:38,360 --> 00:10:02,000
Ryei, would you mind if we sat down to eat with you?

160
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:06,700
Suit yourself.

161
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:10,840
Your Terran food is wonderful.

162
00:10:11,620 --> 00:10:14,360
Unusual and delicious dishes we don't have on verse.

163
00:10:15,900 --> 00:10:17,400
Is that optical camouflage?

164
00:10:17,900 --> 00:10:18,080
Huh?

165
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:22,720
Inaho's friend Nina was kind enough to allow me to borrow these for the time being.

166
00:10:23,140 --> 00:10:26,560
She said it must not have been easy trying to walk through the ship in that dress.

167
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:30,580
Isn't she kind?

168
00:10:30,580 --> 00:10:34,520
Excuse me, your highness.

169
00:10:35,340 --> 00:10:36,440
These are for you.

170
00:10:36,940 --> 00:10:38,160
Oh, just look at them.

171
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:40,820
Paper models of lovely Terran birds.

172
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:42,300
Thank you greatly.

173
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:44,000
I'll treasure them always.

174
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:47,080
That was more thoughtful than I would have expected from you commoners.

175
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:52,580
We shall make a point of this to his imperial majesty when we once again have peace between the earth and...

176
00:10:52,580 --> 00:11:02,440
Martians are known to everyone as the enemy.

177
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:02,460
Martians are known to everyone as the enemy.

178
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:05,340
How can you stay so composed?

179
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:07,880
Even though they were plotting your death.

180
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:11,960
You're insane.

181
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:13,040
Mind your tongue!

182
00:11:13,160 --> 00:11:15,360
How dare you say such a thing to her, royal highness!

183
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:18,380
And I thought we were on the same side.

184
00:11:19,020 --> 00:11:19,400
Hey!

185
00:11:19,540 --> 00:11:21,140
You come back here right now!

186
00:11:21,140 --> 00:11:24,200
Oh, these Terrans are so uncivilized!

187
00:11:28,540 --> 00:11:29,820
How are you feeling, okay?

188
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:32,660
Well, so far, I feel fine.

189
00:11:32,980 --> 00:11:35,960
I recreated the scene based on what you described to me, Lieutenant.

190
00:11:36,580 --> 00:11:40,180
I think it should be pretty close, but if I got something wrong, let me know, alright?

191
00:11:40,580 --> 00:11:42,640
You really think this little gizmo can help?

192
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:44,420
P-T-S-D.

193
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:48,820
There's one treatment that worked pretty well for post-traumatic stress disorder.

194
00:11:48,820 --> 00:11:54,140
It involved trying to recreate the incident that caused it and then reliving it over and over.

195
00:11:54,540 --> 00:11:58,260
Go through a terrifying experience often enough and get acclimated to it, huh?

196
00:11:58,260 --> 00:12:01,360
Well, we'll see how it goes.

197
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:02,740
Why don't we begin?

198
00:12:04,020 --> 00:12:05,040
Yeah, alright.

199
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:08,780
And here we go.

200
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:13,600
Come on.

201
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:16,380
Even games look a lot more real than this these days.

202
00:12:16,540 --> 00:12:17,540
That I wouldn't know.

203
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:19,340
But we're not playing a game.

204
00:12:19,340 --> 00:12:22,280
Ah, you got this street flip from right to left.

205
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:23,920
I'll get that fixed for next time.

206
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:27,920
What is that down there?

207
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:29,800
That's your crewmate, Humoray.

208
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:31,400
Oh, come on now.

209
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:32,280
Give me a break.

210
00:12:32,380 --> 00:12:35,420
I can tell you for a fact what's eating at me ain't a crash test dummy.

211
00:12:35,480 --> 00:12:36,600
Hey, you gotta trust me.

212
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:38,400
Just be quiet and keep watching.

213
00:12:38,620 --> 00:12:39,420
Come on, Doc.

214
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:39,800
Really?

215
00:12:40,040 --> 00:12:41,040
Are you messing with me?

216
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:45,640
Wait a minute.

217
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:48,040
No, that's...

218
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:50,680
Marito!

219
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:54,000
What the hell is that?

220
00:12:54,300 --> 00:12:56,200
Nobody said there'd be anything like that.

221
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:57,080
Hold it together.

222
00:12:57,300 --> 00:12:58,740
We got that thing outnumbered.

223
00:12:59,060 --> 00:13:00,660
Platoon commander to all tanks.

224
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:01,580
Attack formation!

225
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,200
What is that?

226
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:09,000
Marito!

227
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:13,400
That thing's doing this?

228
00:13:16,780 --> 00:13:17,940
It flies?

229
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:22,500
Our shells, they're...

230
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:23,380
Marito!

231
00:13:23,700 --> 00:13:24,760
Anti-gravity?

232
00:13:25,100 --> 00:13:25,420
No!

233
00:13:27,420 --> 00:13:28,300
No!

234
00:13:28,300 --> 00:13:42,900
The tanks have lost cause.

235
00:13:43,780 --> 00:13:45,140
Humoray, we gotta get out!

236
00:13:45,140 --> 00:13:46,240
I can't!

237
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:48,140
My legs are pinned!

238
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:49,980
Fire!

239
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:50,740
Humoray!

240
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:51,360
Marito!

241
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:52,800
Get me out, Marito!

242
00:13:56,940 --> 00:13:57,580
Marito!

243
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:58,640
Marito!

244
00:13:58,840 --> 00:13:59,780
Hurry, Marito!

245
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:03,840
Marito!

246
00:14:04,300 --> 00:14:05,000
Shoot me!

247
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:05,900
Shoot!

248
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:07,800
Please!

249
00:14:08,180 --> 00:14:08,620
Marito!

250
00:14:09,060 --> 00:14:09,460
Hurry!

251
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:10,460
Hurry!

252
00:14:11,260 --> 00:14:12,520
Shoot me, Marito!

253
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:13,240
No!

254
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:13,300
Oh!

255
00:14:13,980 --> 00:14:14,140
Ah!

256
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:22,320
Whoa!

257
00:14:22,740 --> 00:14:31,220
Ohh!

258
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:36,140
Oh!

259
00:14:36,140 --> 00:14:36,880
Oh!

260
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:37,280
Oh!

261
00:14:37,280 --> 00:14:37,820
Oh!

262
00:14:37,820 --> 00:14:38,120
Oh!

263
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:38,140
Oh!

264
00:14:38,140 --> 00:14:53,980
Lieutenant, Lieutenant Marito, calm down. You're all right.

265
00:14:55,820 --> 00:14:59,860
It's okay. You were just remembering the past. You're completely safe.

266
00:15:00,180 --> 00:15:02,300
You're not on Tanegashima anymore.

267
00:15:02,300 --> 00:15:08,820
